 - The `users` array contains the current page of results; if there are more users, follow the `Link` response header with `rel="next"`
 
 To change who has access, use `PUT /:account_slug/boards/:board_id` with the `user_ids` parameter.
+
+## Board Publication
+
+Only account admins and owners with access to the board can publish or unpublish it. Being the board's creator alone does not grant this permission.
+
+### `POST /:account_slug/boards/:board_id/publication`
+
+Publishes the board at a secret public URL. No request body is required. Returns `204 No Content` on success. Fetch the board to obtain its `public_url`.
+
+Publishing an already published board leaves its URL unchanged.
+
+### `DELETE /:account_slug/boards/:board_id/publication`
+
+Unpublishes the board and revokes its public URL, including direct links to its columns and cards. Returns `204 No Content` on success. The board's `public_url` becomes `null`. Publishing the board again generates a new URL; old links remain invalid.
+
+### Public pages
+
+Anyone with the secret URL can view these read-only HTML pages without signing in:
+
+- `GET /:account_slug/public/boards/:key`
+- `GET /:account_slug/public/boards/:key/columns/:id`
+- `GET /:account_slug/public/boards/:key/cards/:number`
+
+Only published cards are visible; drafts are never listed or accessible through public links. Columns and cards must belong to the board identified by the key. Invalid or revoked keys return `404 Not Found`.
diff --git a/test/controllers/boards/publications_controller_test.rb b/test/controllers/boards/publications_controller_test.rb
